{"content":[{"c":["LINTEL*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Horizontal beam placed above a doorway, supported by structures called “jambs” or simply “doorposts.”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.12.1-51","r":"Exod.12.1-51","rawR":"Exod.12.1-51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.12.1-51","value":"Exod.12.1-51"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exodus 12"},", the Israelites are instructed to prepare for the tenth plague, the plague of death, and for the first Passover. After killing a lamb, the people were to take the blood and “put it on the two doorposts and the lintel of the houses” (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.12.7","r":"Exod.12.7","rawR":"Exod.12.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.12.7","value":"Exod.12.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 12:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.6.31","r":"1Kgs.6.31","rawR":"1Kgs.6.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.6.31","value":"1Kgs.6.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"First Kings 6:31"}," describes Solomon’s building of the temple. The ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," says, “He made doors of olive tree: the lintel and side posts were a fifth part of the wall.” The meaning in the Hebrew is a little difficult to determine. The ",{"c":["nasb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," translates it as “the lintel and five-sided doorposts.” The ",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," replaces the word “lintel” with “pilasters.” It may be that the top of the doorway was slanted, formed by beams leaning toward each other (archlike) instead of one horizontal beam."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["In ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.9.1","r":"Amos.9.1","rawR":"Amos.9.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.9.1","value":"Amos.9.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Amos 9:1"}," the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," has “lintel,” whereas the ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," has “capital.” The Hebrew word here appears to mean the capital of a column. The same is true in ",{"href":"?bref=Zeph.2.14","r":"Zeph.2.14","rawR":"Zeph.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zeph.2.14","value":"Zeph.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zephaniah 2:14"},", where the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," has “lintels” and the ",{"c":["nasb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," has “tops of her pillars.” ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Architecture"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Lintel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Exodus 12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.12.1-51","rawQueryValue":"Exod.12.1-51","sourceRefExact":"Exod.12.1-51"},{"anchorText":"Ex 12:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.12.7","rawQueryValue":"Exod.12.7","sourceRefExact":"Exod.12.7"},{"anchorText":"First Kings 6:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.6.31","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.6.31","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.6.31"},{"anchorText":"Amos 9:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.9.1","rawQueryValue":"Amos.9.1","sourceRefExact":"Amos.9.1"},{"anchorText":"Zephaniah 2:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zeph.2.14","rawQueryValue":"Zeph.2.14","sourceRefExact":"Zeph.2.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"739bf799b1f8cae111f0d5e9fa6ecfe6a00286c91ac83ba2e3c8d76f55633758","sourceItemName":"Lintel","sourceItemOrder":105,"sourceMember":"Articles/L.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lintel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Lintel*","title":"Lintel*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}